# Generated-code markers — keeps codegen output out of diff review noise and
# collapsed on GitHub. The generated trees (skeleton design Part 3):
#   proto/gen/**                              — committed Go stubs + generated fakes
#   dataplane/crates/ds-contracts/src/gen/**  — Rust codegen (buf.gen.yaml target)
# Both are produced by the proto/ codegen pipeline; hand edits are forbidden
# (codegen-drift check in .github/workflows/contracts.yml).

proto/gen/** linguist-generated=true -diff
dataplane/crates/ds-contracts/src/gen/** linguist-generated=true -diff

# Keep the hand-written files of generated trees reviewable.
proto/gen/go/go.mod linguist-generated=false diff
proto/gen/go/README.md linguist-generated=false diff
proto/gen/go/doc.go linguist-generated=false diff

# Normalize line endings.
* text=auto

# taskdb task/note store — ID-stable 3-way merge driver. Each task/note is its
# own file keyed by a stable ULID, so concurrent coordinator/cross-machine
# edits to DIFFERENT tasks never conflict, and edits to the SAME task reconcile
# by union (status most-progressed-wins, depends_on unioned, never drop a task
# either side has) instead of clobbering. The driver is `taskdb merge-json`,
# registered per-clone by `taskdb setup` AND self-healed on every taskdb
# invocation when `merge.taskdb.driver` is unset (git never auto-applies a merge
# driver from a clone, so a `git clone --local` worktree that skipped setup would
# otherwise silently fall back to text conflicts). Falls back to text conflicts
# if .bin/taskdb is absent.
tasks/task-*.json merge=taskdb
tasks/note-*.json merge=taskdb
